Fallout 3 was the game that turned me into a fan of the series, it's atmosphere made me see how much I love post-apocalyptic scenarios, in this case it's a ruined Washington D.C. filled with all kinds of dangers, people and oportunities.
The pros:
-A good post-apocalyptic atmosphere that makes you explore more of the wasted capital of the U.S. and really feels like a completely destroyed city;
-Combat is more fluid than in the previous games of the franchise;
-A varied set of characters, quests and whacky moments;
-Your dad is voiced by Liam Neeson;
-You can blow up an entire town with a nuke;
-One of the DLC's allows you to kill funny-sounding aliens on an alien spaceship
The cons:
-Real Time Combat sometimes feels like it doesn't show much impact and enemies look like they're being hit with teeny bits of paper when you shoot at them and almost show no pain with the impact unless you cripple them;
-Not a big variety of weapons and calibers compared to the previous and posterior titles of the franchise (although you can always put mods in it);
-Short level cap of 30;
-(SPOILER ALERT) The main story only has 2 outcomes and the ending cinematic doesn't show what impact you had on the capital wasteland besides if you turned on project purity or sent someone else to do it and if you injected the poison on the system or not;

