I'll be short : 7/10. Important note: if you're looking for a badass 3rd person action/slasher , like devs' previous title DMC - you're in the wrong place. This is a narrative-driven puzzle-solver mostly, with absolutely stunning visuals and deep and great story if you actually try to dive into it.
Pros :
-Amazing graphics;
-Amazing sound;
-Interesting and captivating story;
-Fluid, responsive, and beautiful combat;
Cons :
- Dozens of SAME REPETITIVE puzzles in which you need to find Runes to open doors. Sometimes minor details are changed, but at its core - puzzles are 99% the same, which makes it a chore, not really fun.
Overall :
Rollercoaster. Super boring puzzles interchanging with super amazing combat, cutscenes, etc etc. But beaing an avid reader - I love narrative based games, and the story in this one is amazing.

Wow, okay, wasn't expecting what I got out of this game. I wanted a game with a good story and gameplay, and while those delivered, I also got beautiful graphics and an overall cathartic feeling after finishing it-- not to mention the outstanding music, oh my god. I really loved this game and I can't find much to say against it.
Would I recommend it? Yes, of course. One of the best sidescrollers I've ever played. Ever.
Oh, but I would like to know who hurt the designer of the chase scenes ;-;

